Z||000005||Slammed Fiero||10-25-2001||10:35 PM||||I have never even used it. It doesn't really suit my purposes and I could better spend money elsewhere.<P>Not some hack job , it's the Proper NOS kit for a 60 degree V6. Forum member Shaun41178 ran the same kit on his Fiero for quite a while with no problems. Mines jetted to 70hp , I believe shaun ran his at 90hp a few times, and I know he used the juice a lot.<P>To be honest I never got around to trying it , I have been so busy this summer with school. I did a really nice install job , I hid all the switches used proper connectors , made a TB bracket out of aluminum to mount the Micro switch.<P>I'm not actively trying to sell it. I don't really need the money , but if someone wants to buy it , I will sell.<P>It would cost you around $700 to duplicate the setup , it also has the bottle gauge.  If no one has interest in Buying it , I will leave it in and probably fill it next spring and hit the strip a few times.<P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000006||TRiAD||10-25-2001||11:23 PM||||I'll soon be starting an Eaton Supercharger kit for the 2.8. <P>Looking for 100HP increase for no more than $3K. <P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg"> <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I>||||reg||1
